2
00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:19,840
Sorry—hello?

3
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:23,900
Yes, I can hear you now. Giỏi, you can begin the training session.

4
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:33,210
First of all, thank you all for joining today's sharing session.

5
00:01:33,210 --> 00:01:41,310
My name is Giỏi, and today I will share what I know about GTest.

6
00:01:41,310 --> 00:01:46,910
Please share any comments that can help improve today's session.

7
00:01:46,910 --> 00:01:56,196
This morning, I will cover four topics: an overview of GTest,

8
00:01:56,196 --> 00:02:04,416
the GTest Automation Tool, software environment setup,

9
00:02:04,416 --> 00:02:07,460
and a Q&A session.

10
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:09,312
Based on what I have learned,

11
00:02:09,312 --> 00:02:12,696
GTest is an open-source framework released by Google,

12
00:02:12,696 --> 00:02:14,420
hence the name Google Test.

13
00:02:14,420 --> 00:02:38,620
It supports code testing and provides a framework for Unit Testing.

14
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:42,589
It is similar to Cantata,

15
00:02:42,589 --> 00:02:53,860
but it is lightweight and supports several utilities defined by Google.

16
00:02:53,860 --> 00:03:10,630
Its management capabilities and overall flexibility are very strong.

17
00:03:10,630 --> 00:03:12,470
With a Cantata test,

18
00:03:12,470 --> 00:03:17,530
we need to configure many prerequisites for it to work.

19
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:24,550
With GTest, the setup is not that complex; it is much simpler.

20
00:03:24,550 --> 00:03:29,152
We will cover this in more detail in the next sessions.

21
00:03:29,152 --> 00:03:32,080
The goal is to shorten testing time

22
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:34,421
and increase efficiency.

23
00:03:34,421 --> 00:03:40,370
Does anyone have any questions or comments about Google Test?

24
00:03:40,370 --> 00:03:54,400
Now, why should we use Google Test for Unit Testing?

25
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:59,497
It is highly reusable,

26
00:03:59,497 --> 00:04:05,793
lets us test each test case independently,

27
00:04:05,793 --> 00:04:11,040
and reduces the size of test files.

28
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:13,146
From using it,

29
00:04:13,146 --> 00:04:20,308
I found that applying GTest to our project greatly shortens the time

30
00:04:20,308 --> 00:04:24,100
required and increases productivity.

31
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:35,940
Previously, our team created many GTest test cases.

32
00:04:35,940 --> 00:04:41,512
As the test suite grows,

33
00:04:41,512 --> 00:04:58,460
we add new test cases only when new issues or code changes need coverage.

34
00:04:58,460 --> 00:05:06,060
Next is an overview of the GTest Automation Tool.

35
00:05:06,060 --> 00:05:15,306
You can search online for information about this tool,

36
00:05:15,306 --> 00:05:20,100
or use the link copied here.

37
00:05:20,100 --> 00:05:29,837
It is a prebuilt tool; we only need to download and use it.

38
00:05:29,837 --> 00:05:40,234
It supports several features, including test cases and reports,

39
00:05:40,234 --> 00:05:45,680
and retains relevant information.

40
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:59,781
Please read the documentation to understand it more fully.

41
00:05:59,781 --> 00:06:12,910
We will move quickly to the next, more important part.

42
00:06:12,910 --> 00:06:27,100
We will now set up the software environment so that we can run GTest.

43
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:38,853
On your computer, install Visual Studio Code and TCC.

44
00:06:38,853 --> 00:06:51,050
TCC contains the compiler; we use MinGW to build GTest.

45
00:06:51,050 --> 00:06:59,240
TCC can be installed from the IT server or the internal portal.

46
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:10,444
For the GTest Automation Tool, there are two ways to download it:

47
00:07:10,444 --> 00:07:18,718
run Installer.bat with the required permissions,

48
00:07:18,718 --> 00:07:26,820
or download the GTest Automation Tool ZIP file.

49
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:38,250
These are the steps for installing TCC and Visual Studio Code.

50
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:44,887
Please use the version at this link,

51
00:07:44,887 --> 00:07:52,630
which matches the project I am working on.

52
00:07:52,630 --> 00:08:00,961
Please download the version of the GTest Automation Tool at this link

53
00:08:00,961 --> 00:08:04,463
